  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0083 database is designed to manage various aspects of a customer support system, including conversations, emails, users, and settings. The database consists of 19 tables, each representing a specific entity or concept. The activity_logs table stores records of system activities, including log names, descriptions, and timestamps. The attachments table contains information about uploaded files, such as their directory, name, type, and size, and is linked to the threads and users tables. The conversation_folder table establishes relationships between conversations and folders, while the conversations table stores details about individual conversations, including their number, type, status, and participants. The customers table holds information about customers, including their name, email, and contact details, and is linked to the emails and conversations tables. The emails table stores email addresses associated with customers, and the folders table manages mailboxes and their contents. The followers table tracks users who follow specific conversations, and the ltm_translations table stores translations for the system. The mailbox_user table links mailboxes to users, and the mailboxes table stores settings for mailboxes, including their name, email, and configuration. The modules table manages system modules, and the notifications table stores notifications sent to users. The options table stores system settings, and the polycast_events table logs events in the system. The send_logs table tracks sent emails, and the subscriptions table manages user subscriptions to events. The threads table stores information about individual threads, including their conversation ID, user ID, and status, and is linked to the conversations and users tables. Finally, the users table stores information about system users, including their name, email, password, and permissions.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nFreeScout is an open-source help desk and shared inbox solution, designed as a lightweight alternative to commercial customer support applications like Zendesk and Help Scout. Built using the Laravel PHP framework, FreeScout offers flexibility through an extensive module system, allowing customization of its features. It enables organizations to manage customer support independently, without privacy concerns or dependency on third-party services.\n\n Objectives\n\nThe primary objective is to provide a cost-effective, self-hosted help desk solution that is customizable and fully-featured, ensuring users maintain control over their data.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Support Agents: Manage customer interactions, respond to queries, and track conversation statuses.\n- Administrators: Customize and configure the platform, manage users, and oversee overall system operations.\n- Customers: Communicate with support agents via email or integrated platforms like Slack or WhatsApp.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n\n- Agent Management: Support for unlimited agents and mailboxes.\n- Communication: Starred conversations, seamless email integration, auto-replies, internal notes, and conversation forwarding and merging.\n- Notifications & Tracking: Push notifications, conversation following, collision detection, and open tracking.\n- User Interaction Features: Multilingual support, keyboard shortcuts, mentions, and screen reader accessibility.\n- Integration & Automation: Integrations with Slack, WhatsApp, Facebook, Telegram, LDAP, email commands, and Kanban boards.\n- Conversation Management: Auto-refreshing conversation lists, saving replies, satisfaction ratings, spam filtering, and conversation tagging.\n- Security & Privacy: Built with a strong focus on security and privacy.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: Lightweight system design for efficient performance with minimal resource usage.\n- Scalability: Ability to handle an unlimited number of tickets and customer interactions.\n- Accessibility: Supports screen readers and provides a mobile-friendly interface.\n- Usability: Easy web installer and integration of multiple communication channels for enhanced user experience.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0083.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0083\nCREATE TABLE `activity_logs` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `log_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `timestamp` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `attachments` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `directory` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `size` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `attachments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `conversation_folder` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `conversation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `folder_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `conversation_folder_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`conversation_id`) REFERENCES `conversations` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `conversation_folder_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`folder_id`) REFERENCES `folders` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `conversations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customers` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_details` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `emails` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `email_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `emails_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `folders` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `followers` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `conversation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `followers_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `followers_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`conversation_id`) REFERENCES `conversations` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ltm_translations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `key` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `value` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `mailbox_user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `mailbox_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `mailbox_user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`mailbox_id`) REFERENCES `mailboxes` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `mailbox_user_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `mailboxes` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `configuration` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `modules` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notifications` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message` text NOT NULL,\n  `timestamp` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `notifications_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `options` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `key` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `value` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `polycast_events` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `event_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `timestamp` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `send_logs` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `timestamp` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `send_logs_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`email_id`) REFERENCES `emails` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `subscriptions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `event_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscriptions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `threads` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `conversation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `threads_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`conversation_id`) REFERENCES `conversations` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `threads_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `permissions` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
